  "notes": [
    "HAND-ASSEMBLED. tu_map.py has no candidate for this range (see boundary_evidence item 2), so `tubuild.py create` could not be used; the schema still comes from tubuild.build_manifest_entry.",
    "Reconciliation is documented in the source file's own header comment. Summary: 9 shadow type names dropped in favour of real headers, 9 globals/prototypes given one spelling each, one local type renamed, and a handful of casts and field renames that follow from those. Nothing changes what a function does.",
    "include/Actor.h gained `struct Matrix4x3;`, `void UntrackInDeathTable();` and `Matrix4x3 *UpdateCarry(Player &, const Vector3 &);` -- all non-virtual, so the 0xd0 size assertion and the 31 vtable slots are unchanged and ~Actor() is still the key function.",
    "Actor::~Actor is deliberately NOT defined as a method here. include/Actor.h's own comment states the invariant: the key function must never be defined as a real method or the TU emits _ZTV8dActor_c and collides with the gap object's copy. D0, D1 and D2 keep their extern \"C\" free-function form.",
    "This TU also owns, and this round neither declares nor verifies, _ZTV8dActor_c (0x0208e3a4, 31 slots), _ZTI8dActor_c/_ZTS8dActor_c and whatever .data/.bss the range's globals live in. Nothing here is enrolled; config/arm9/delinks.txt is untouched and the 97 one-function sources under src/ remain the owners of the range.",
    "LINK-VERIFIED, whole range, from ONE object: `tubuild.py linkcheck arm9/Actor` reports the .text range 0x0200f658..0x02011654 (8,188 bytes) IDENTICAL, module fidelity 106/106 exact at 100.000000%, 10,905/10,905 source-built functions reproducing with 0 mismatching, `dsd check modules --fail` PASS, and a ROM whose sha256 is d1506e90efae5e2d2cf119926a4ac2a291bd5ca78349d09d5024e1a918c478e8 -- the SAME hash `linkcheck --baseline` produces with no substitution at all.",
    "`dsd check symbols --fail` is NOT green and is not reported as such: it fails on data_020ad524 and data_020ad560. The baseline control emits those same two, and linkcheck reports `0 NEW, 0 resolved` against it, so they are the tree's and not this TU's -- but the check is red.",
    "ONE unlicensed .text body remains: _ZN7Vector3D1Ev, 4 bytes, STB_LOPROC, already defined at arm9:0x020072c0. The audit classes it COLLIDES-SRC, tolerated only while both definitions are vague-linkage, which they are. It is emitted because include/types.h gives Vector3 an inline empty destructor and this TU instantiates Vector3 arrays; the same body comes out of the legacy per-function objects today. Promotion is still refused on it.",
    "THE ONE DELIBERATE DEPARTURE FROM THE LEGACY SOURCE, and it is the whole reason the whole-range link passes. Ordinal 95, _ZN8Vector3sD1Ev at 0x02011508, spells its mangled ROM symbol directly (`extern \"C\" void _ZN8Vector3sD1Ev(void *) {}`) rather than going through src/runtime/math/Vector3s/_ZN8Vector3sD1Ev.cpp's Vector3s_ForceDestructor scaffold. types.h defines ~Vector3s() INLINE, so an out-of-line copy can only be forced by making the compiler destroy an ARRAY of it -- and that scaffold is 0x50 of STB_GLOBAL .text (D1 and D2, 0x28 each) that no symbols.txt anywhere names. Per-function objisolate strips it; a merged object cannot, `-nodead` keeps it, and it lands INSIDE the span. Measured with the scaffold in place: TU range 506 bytes DIFFER from 0x0200f670 on, 15/106 modules exact, 540,285 module bytes differing. Measured without it: range IDENTICAL, 106/106 exact. Same four bytes either way.",
    "COST OF THAT DEPARTURE, stated rather than hidden: the object-level partial-isolation axis drops to 96/97. The one miss is _ZN8Vector3sD1Ev and it is a symbol BINDING difference on four byte-identical bytes -- production STB_LOPROC (vague linkage, which is what the scaffold produces) vs derived STB_GLOBAL (a strong definition, which is what the ROM's single copy at 0x02011508 actually is). `linkcheck --partial` still builds the identical ROM hash and 106/106 exact modules with it. With the scaffold instead, partial isolation is 97/97 and the whole-range link fails; the two cannot both be had, and link-verified is the higher rung.",
    "The pre-scaffold-removal measurements are reproducible: put the Vector3s_ForceDestructor form back for ordinal 95 and the object audit reports 97 LICENSED / 1 COLLIDES-SRC / 2 HOMELESS with the PREDICTION that the two STB_GLOBAL bodies cannot be deadstripped under -nodead.",
    "include/Actor.h's three new declarations were re-verified against the tree, not assumed safe: all 1,126 src/ files that transitively include Actor.h were rebuilt under build_pin.verify. 1,124 reproduce; the 2 that do not (_ZN15daObjMarioCap_c13InitResourcesEv, _ZN15RollingIronBall13InitResourcesEv) fail identically with the header reverted to HEAD~1 and carry no `complete` marker, so they are neither enrolled nor this change's.",
    "STILL NOT DONE, and not claimed: `promoted`. config/**/delinks.txt is untouched, the 97 one-function sources under src/ remain the enrolled owners of the range, and this TU's data side -- _ZTV8dActor_c (0x0208e3a4, 31 slots), _ZTI8dActor_c/_ZTS8dActor_c and whatever .data/.bss its globals live in -- is neither declared nor verified here."
